gcrosswhite wrote:
> 
> Some people consider healers to be a particularly difficult class with
> which to ascend. 

You have to play them slightly different. (Incidentally, my own first
NAO ascension was a neutral gnomish healer as well.)

> I however think that they are actually one of the
> easier ones to ascend with if you have the protection racket. 

Even without that you have a lot of interesting options with healers;
the stethoscope is *very* nice, and all the healing spells and potions
keep you alive, if you know in time when to retreat.

The problem with the protection racket is that you can easily kill
many characters before you get a lucky one. Relying on your pet alone
(which may die, so that you're at your own without enough HPs) is not
a good strategy. I assume PR players typically don't mind if their
characters die early, because they can immediately start a new one
without having invested too much time and effort. And once the healers
are beyond the early game (by a successful PR or otherwise) they are
not bad.

